<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William II of England</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1056–<a href="/years/1100">1100</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as William Rufus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William II, called Rufus, was the third son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-conqueror">William the Conqueror</a> and king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> from 1087. He put down rebellions by barons who favoured his elder brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-curthose">Robert Curthose</a>, and in 1096 took Normandy in pledge from Robert, who was leaving on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-crusade">First Crusade</a>. He was killed by an arrow while hunting in the New Forest in 1100 and was succeeded by his brother Henry I.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-ii-of-england.jpg" alt="William II of England" width="320" height="497" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Matthew Paris · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:William_II_of_England_Historia_Anglorum.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
